# c-testsuite baseline — contains ONLY cases outside zcc's C99 scope.
#
# ── 00219: _Generic ──
# The case uses _Generic (C11 6.5.1.1) — NOT part of C99. zcc, being strict C99, rejects it
# correctly (reporting "undeclared variable: int" at `_Generic(a, int: ...)`). The referee
# `cc -std=c99` SWALLOWS _Generic as a GNU extension ⇒ the oracle is UNSOUND (the referee
# evaluates a c99+GNU superset, not the strict c99 of the compiler-under-test). Same
# class as the referee-standard lesson: a diff on a feature outside standard S is meaningless.
# Not a bug; if a later milestone acquires _Generic, remove this entry.
FAIL 00219
